"value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}I-\\frac{1}{2}A-\\frac{3}{2}{A}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3b9ca1f0e5e88294dd232877ed23203a149809a11e92ceac8c681f06ab8309f" "basis" 2382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-40168" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{2}I-\\frac{7}{2}A-\\frac{1}{2}{A}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3b9ca1f0e5e88294dd232877ed23203a149809a11e92ceac8c681f06ab8309f" "basis" 2382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-40168" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7}{2}I-\\frac{1}{2}A-\\frac{1}{2}{A}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3b9ca1f0e5e88294dd232877ed23203a149809a11e92ceac8c681f06ab8309f" "basis" 2382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-140531" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}],$ then ${A}^{-1}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3b9ca1f0e5e88294dd232877ed23203a149809a11e92ceac8c681f06ab8309f" "basis" 2382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-140531" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's find the characteristic equation $\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )((2-\\lambda )(-3-\\lambda )-2) & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -8) & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}-11\\lambda +24 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{3}-2{A}^{2}-11A+24I & =O.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A$ is invertible, we can multiply this equation by ${A}^{-1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}({A}^{3}-2{A}^{2}-11A+24I) & =O \\\\ {A}^{2}-2A-11I+24{A}^{-1} & =O \\\\ 24{A}^{-1} & =11I+2A-{A}^{2} \\\\ {A}^{-1} & =\\frac{11}{24}I+\\frac{1}{12}A-\\frac{1}{24}{A}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3b9ca1f0e5e88294dd232877ed23203a149809a11e92ceac8c681f06ab8309f" "basis" 2382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-140531" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "52afb5275bd0959a2d515d3f40a045f29dca7f07c8dc62c8195a0317cd10c970" "basis" 2382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-140531" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3b9ca1f0e5e88294dd232877ed23203a149809a11e92ceac8c681f06ab8309f" "basis" 2382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-140531" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "24I+\\frac{1}{12}A+\\frac{1}{6}{A}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3b9ca1f0e5e88294dd232877ed23203a149809a11e92ceac8c681f06ab8309f" "basis" 2382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-140531" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{11}{12}I+\\frac{1}{3}A-\\frac{1}{24}{A}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3b9ca1f0e5e88294dd232877ed23203a149809a11e92ceac8c681f06ab8309f" "basis" 2382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-140531" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{11}{24}I+\\frac{1}{12}A+\\frac{1}{12}{A}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3b9ca1f0e5e88294dd232877ed23203a149809a11e92ceac8c681f06ab8309f" "basis" 2382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-140531" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{11}{24}I+\\frac{1}{12}A-\\frac{1}{24}{A}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3b9ca1f0e5e88294dd232877ed23203a149809a11e92ceac8c681f06ab8309f" "basis" 2382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-140531" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{11}{24}I-\\frac{1}{6}A+\\frac{1}{24}{A}^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3b9ca1f0e5e88294dd232877ed23203a149809a11e92ceac8c681f06ab8309f" "basis" 2382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-140531" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{11}{24}I+\\frac{1}{12}A-\\frac{1}{24}{A}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/state.json" "file_sha256" "b3b9ca1f0e5e88294dd232877ed23203a149809a11e92ceac8c681f06ab8309f" "basis" 2382 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069543/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-38705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ with characteristic polynomial $p(x)={x}^{2}-2x-8,$ then ${A}^{3}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070368/state.json" "file_sha256" "14f09b79539e6b074951ce88533b6d2cbe2efb18f2185400e33f0c2d38d15559"} {"question" "q-38705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's divide the polynomial $f(x)={x}^{3}$ by characteristic polynomial $p(x)={x}^{2}-2x-8,$ using long division:\n\n|  | $\\,\\,x$ | $+$ | $2$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}^{2}-2x-8\\,$ | $\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{{x}^{3}\\,\\,}$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | $-$ | $2{x}^{2}$ | $-$ | $8x$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  | $2{x}^{2}$ | $+$ | $8x$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  | $2{x}^{2}$ | $-$ | $4x$ | $-$ | $16$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  |  | $12x$ | $+$ | $16$ |  |  |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we can write ${x}^{3}$ as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3} & =q(x)p(x)+(12x+16),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $q(x)=x+2.$  Replacing $x$ with $A,$ we have\n\n$$\n{A}^{3}=q(A)p(A)+(12A+16I).\n$$\n\nNow, according to the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have $p(A)=O.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{3} & =q(A)p(A)+(12A+16I) \\\\  & =q(A)\\cdot O+(12A+16I) \\\\  & =12A+16I.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070368/state.json" "file_sha256" "14f09b79539e6b074951ce88533b6d2cbe2efb18f2185400e33f0c2d38d15559"} {"question" "q-38705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070368/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4590011cfe49e93c245b73372559946c39dfec009f293061a002756330345b30"} {"question" "q-38705" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070368/state.json" "file_sha256" "14f09b79539e6b074951ce88533b6d2cbe2efb18f2185400e33f0c2d38d15559"} {"question" "q-38705" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-12A-16I"] ["math" "12A+16I"] ["math" "16A-12I"] ["math" "2A+6I"] ["math" "2A+I"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070368/state.json" "file_sha256" "14f09b79539e6b074951ce88533b6d2cbe2efb18f2185400e33f0c2d38d15559"} {"question" "q-38705" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12A+16I"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070368/state.json" "file_sha256" "14f09b79539e6b074951ce88533b6d2cbe2efb18f2185400e33f0c2d38d15559"} {"question" "q-38723" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $A$ be a $3\\times 3$ matrix with the characteristic polynomial $p(\\lambda )=-{\\lambda }^{3}-2\\lambda -1.$ Then, ${A}^{3}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070368/state.json" "file_sha256" "14f09b79539e6b074951ce88533b6d2cbe2efb18f2185400e33f0c2d38d15559"} {"question" "q-38723" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(A) & =O \\\\ -{A}^{3}-2A-I & =O \\\\ {A}^{3} & =-2A-I.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070368/state.json" "file_sha256" "14f09b79539e6b074951ce88533b6d2cbe2efb18f2185400e33f0c2d38d15559"} {"question" "q-38723" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070368/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4590011cfe49e93c245b73372559946c39dfec009f293061a002756330345b30"} {"question" "q-38723" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070368/state.json" "file_sha256" "14f09b79539e6b074951ce88533b6d2cbe2efb18f2185400e33f0c2d38d15559"} {"question" "q-38723" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2A+{A}^{2}"] ["math" "-2A-I"] ["math" "-2{A}^{2}-A"] ["math" "-2{A}^{2}-I"] ["math" "2A-I"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070368/state.json" "file_sha256" "14f09b79539e6b074951ce88533b6d2cbe2efb18f2185400e33f0c2d38d15559"} {"question" "q-38723" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2A-I"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070368/state.json" "file_sha256" "14f09b79539e6b074951ce88533b6d2cbe2efb18f2185400e33f0c2d38d15559"} {"question" "q-38728" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the matrix\n$\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 11 \\\\ -3 & -6\\end{aligned}]$\nand $f(x)={x}^{15}-3{x}^{13}+{x}^{3}-5x+6$, find $f(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070368/state.json" "file_sha256" "14f09b79539e6b074951ce88533b6d2cbe2efb18f2185400e33f0c2d38d15559"} {"question" "q-38728" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's start by finding the characteristic polynomial $p(\\lambda )$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & =\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}6-\\lambda  & 11 \\\\ -3 & -6-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(6-\\lambda )(-6-\\lambda )+33 \\\\  & ={\\lambda }^{2}-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's divide $f(x)$ by $p(x)$ using long division:\n\n|  | $\\,\\,{x}^{13}$ | $+$ | $x$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}^{2}-3\\,$ | $\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{{x}^{15}-3{x}^{13}+{x}^{3}-5x+6}$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | ${x}^{15}$ | $\\,\\,\\,\\,-$ | $\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{13}$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  | ${x}^{3}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$ | $-\\,\\,$ | $\\,\\,5x$ | $\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,+$ | $\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6$ |\n|  |  |  |  | ${x}^{3}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$ | $-\\,\\,$ | $\\,\\,3x$ |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  |  | $-\\,\\,$ | $\\,\\,2x$ | $\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,+$ | $\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6$ |\n\nTherefore, we can write $f(x)$ as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =q(x)p(x)+r(x) \\\\  & =q(x)p(x)+(-2x+6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $q(x)={x}^{13}+x.$ Replacing $x$ with $A,$ we have\n\n$$\nf(A)=q(A)p(A)+(-2A+6I).\n$$\n\nAccording to the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have $p(A)=O.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & =q(A)p(A)+(-2A+6I) \\\\  & =q(A)\\cdot O+(-2A+6I) \\\\  & =-2A+6I \\\\  & =-2[\\begin{aligned}6 & 11 \\\\ -3 & -6\\end{aligned}]+6[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-12 & -22 \\\\ 6 & 12\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -22 \\\\ 6 & 18\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070368/state.json" "file_sha256" "14f09b79539e6b074951ce88533b6d2cbe2efb18f2185400e33f0c2d38d15559"} {"question" "q-38728" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070368/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4590011cfe49e93c245b73372559946c39dfec009f293061a002756330345b30"} {"question" "q-38728" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070368/state.json" "file_sha256" "14f09b79539e6b074951ce88533b6d2cbe2efb18f2185400e33f0c2d38d15559"} {"question" "q-38728" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-12 & -22 \\\\ 6 & 12\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-22 & -6 \\\\ 6 & 18\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -22 \\\\ 18 & 6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -22 \\\\ 6 & 18\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}18 & -22 \\\\ 6 & -6\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070368/state.json" "file_sha256" "14f09b79539e6b074951ce88533b6d2cbe2efb18f2185400e33f0c2d38d15559"} {"question" "q-38728" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -22 \\\\ 6 & 18\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070368/state.json" "file_sha256" "14f09b79539e6b074951ce88533b6d2cbe2efb18f2185400e33f0c2d38d15559"} {"question" "q-40168" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],$ then ${A}^{-1}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070368/state.json" "file_sha256" "14f09b79539e6b074951ce88533b6d2cbe2efb18f2185400e33f0c2d38d15559"} {"question" "q-40168" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's find the characteristic equation $\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4-\\lambda  & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-4-\\lambda  & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )((-4-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )+3) & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda -1) & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}+{\\lambda }^{2}-7\\lambda +2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{3}+{A}^{2}-7A+2I & =O.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A$ is invertible, we can multiply this equation by ${A}^{-1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}({A}^{3}+{A}^{2}-7A+2I) & =O \\\\ {A}^{2}+A-7I+2{A}^{-1} & =O \\\\ 2{A}^{-1} & =7I-A-{A}^{2} \\\\ {A}^{-1} & =\\frac{7}{2}I-\\frac{1}{2}A-\\frac{1}{2}{A}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070368/state.json" "file_sha256" "14f09b79539e6b074951ce88533b6d2cbe2efb18f2185400e33f0c2d38d15559"} {"question" "q-40168" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070368/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4590011cfe49e93c245b73372559946c39dfec009f293061a002756330345b30"} {"question" "q-40168" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070368/state.json" "file_sha256" "14f09b79539e6b074951ce88533b6d2cbe2efb18f2185400e33f0c2d38d15559"} {"question" "q-40168" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2I-A-2{A}^{2}"] ["math" "9I-A-{A}^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}I-\\frac{1}{2}A-\\frac{3}{2}{A}^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}I-\\frac{7}{2}A-\\frac{1}{2}{A}^{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{2}I-\\frac{1}{2}A-\\frac{1}{2}{A}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_c